IMPORT prelude

-- Electric Vehicles Charging Act 2022 (Singapore) -- who counts as a charging station operator and when a licence is needed
-- (ss 4(1), 41), charging with an unregistered charger (s 18), registration marks and transfers (ss 20, 21, 27), keeping
-- certificates (s 26), improper use and charging, tampering and labels (ss 29-32), defect warnings (s 36), the maximum
-- penalties for those offences and for ss 6, 23, 24, 39, "repeat offender" (s 2), composition (s 81), the building and
-- electrical-work trigger for charging points in car parks (ss 61, 62, 65(4)) and the appeal window (s 68(2)).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/7/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EVCA2022.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026). Amendment annotations seen: S 795/2023 (wef 8
-- December 2023), Act 5 of 2026 (wef 4 May 2026) and Act 15 of 2026 (wef 1 July 2026, the latest annotated).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance (Tier 1): anyone who owns an EV, installs a home or condo charger,
-- or lives in a building whose car park must be wired for charging meets it. SCOPED to those provisions. Not encoded:
-- homologation and approval labels (ss 7-13), advertising (ss 14-17), specially authorised chargers (s 28) beyond their
-- carve-out, safety directives beyond the penalty (ss 37-38), the licensing scheme beyond s 41 (ss 42-55), step-in
-- (ss 56-59), s 64 building-works duties beyond the trigger, enforcement powers (ss 73-80, 82-87), the Schedule's
-- transitional rules, and everything left to Regulations or Gazette orders (inspection intervals, banned locations,
-- permissible purposes, the charging-point formulas, compoundable offences, exemptions).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electric Vehicles Charging Act 2022 -- charging`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `4(1) and 41 -- charging station operators and unlicensed regulated activity`

-- s 4(1): a charging station operator is a person who (a) operates "in the course of any business" charging stations for use
-- primarily by the general public; (b) operates in the course of any business charging stations for the exclusive use of its
-- employees, outworkers or engaged individuals; or (c) "has charge and control of any charging point in any place in
-- Singapore (whether or not in the course of any business) to charge any electric vehicle for its propulsion unless excluded
-- by the Minister by order in the Gazette".
-- s 2: "regulated activity" means providing EV charging services in Singapore, or "engaging in conduct as a charging station
-- operator".
-- s 41(1): an offence to undertake any regulated activity using a type of EV charger (except a specially authorised EV
-- charger) when (a) not authorised by a licence and (b) not exempt under s 92. (2) "a strict liability offence". (3)
-- individual: $10,000 or 6 months, plus $250 a day continuing; not an individual: $30,000 plus $500 a day.
--
-- Read literally, limb (c) makes a householder with a wall charger a charging station operator unless a Gazette order
-- excludes them; whether one does was not retrieved.
GIVEN `operates public stations in business` IS A BOOLEAN, `operates staff-only stations in business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has charge and control of a charging point` IS A BOOLEAN, `excluded by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a charging station operator` IF
        `operates public stations in business`
    OR  `operates staff-only stations in business`
    OR  (`has charge and control of a charging point` AND (NOT `excluded by Ministerial order`))

GIVEN `undertakes a regulated activity` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt under section 92` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `using a specially authorised charger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unlicensed regulated activity is an offence` IF
    `undertakes a regulated activity` AND (NOT `holds a licence for it`) AND (NOT `exempt under section 92`)
        AND (NOT `using a specially authorised charger`)

GIVEN `offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed regulated activity` MEANS
    IF `offender is an individual`
    THEN 10000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    ELSE 30000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `18 -- charging with an unregistered charger`

-- s 18(1): an offence if the person (a) "charges an electric vehicle using an EV charger"; (b) it is unregistered; (c) "the
-- person knows that, or is reckless as to whether" it is unregistered. (2): the same for a person who "allows an electric
-- vehicle to be charged" with it. (4) "it is immaterial whether the person is a licensee".
-- s 19(1): the person with charge and control "must apply to the LTA to register the EV charger before the EV charger is first
-- used". s 19 itself carries no penalty; s 18 is what bites.
GIVEN `charged or allowed charging` IS A BOOLEAN, `the charger is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `charging with an unregistered charger is an offence` IF
    `charged or allowed charging` AND (NOT `the charger is registered`) AND `knew or was reckless`

§§ `20, 21, 26 -- registration marks and certificates`

-- s 20(2): the registered responsible person must ensure the registration mark "is affixed on that EV charger in the prescribed
-- manner within 60 days after the registration date" (or a longer prescribed period); (3) offence "without reasonable excuse".
-- s 21(2): on cancellation, the mark must be "removed from the EV charger within 30 days after the LTA informs" the person;
-- (4) a fine up to $1,000.
-- s 26(1): keep every fitness certificate under ss 23 and 25(3)(b)(i) "for a period of at least 2 years starting the date the
-- certificate is made"; (3) a fine up to $10,000.
GIVEN `days since registration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration mark is still in time` IF `days since registration` AT MOST 60

GIVEN `days since told of cancellation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mark removal is still in time` IF `days since told of cancellation` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `months since the certificate was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate may be discarded` IF `months since the certificate was made` AT LEAST 24

§§ `27 -- transferring the registration`

-- s 27(1): a registered responsible person who "disposes of, or transfers immediate possession of otherwise than temporarily"
-- must, within a prescribed period, apply to transfer the registration to the transferee.
-- (4): the section "does not apply to the passing of possession" (a) under any hiring "(not being a hiring under a
-- hire-purchase agreement)" or lending; (b) to an agent for sale or destruction; (c) to a bailee for "alteration, repair,
-- renovation, garaging, storing"; (d) under a court order or other legal process; (e) other prescribed circumstances.
DECLARE Handover IS ONE OF
    `selling the charger`
    `giving the charger away`
    `letting it on hire-purchase`
    `hiring it out`
    `lending it`
    `leaving it with an agent to sell`
    `leaving it for repair`
    `handing it over under a court order`

GIVEN `the handover` IS A Handover
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration must be transferred` IF
    CONSIDER `the handover`
    WHEN `selling the charger` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `giving the charger away` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `letting it on hire-purchase` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `29, 30 -- improper use and improper charging`

-- s 30(1): an offence to use, or allow to be used, an EV charger to charge at a place "prescribed as a banned location for that
-- type of EV charger", knowing or reckless; (2) likewise for a way or circumstances not prescribed as permissible.
-- (4): not for a person (a) whose business is to repair EV chargers or to test them against the homologation standards and
-- (b) who uses it "for the sole purpose" of that testing or repair in the ordinary course of business.
GIVEN `charged at a banned location or in an impermissible way` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a repair or testing business` IS A BOOLEAN, `solely to repair or test` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `improper charging is an offence` IF
    `charged at a banned location or in an impermissible way` AND `knew or was reckless`
        AND (NOT (`is a repair or testing business` AND `solely to repair or test`))

§§ `31 -- tampering and negligence`

-- s 31(1): "wilfully tampers with an EV charger ... so as to cause or to be likely to cause danger to human life or damage to any
-- property"; (3) $100,000 or 5 years. (2): "by rash or negligent act or omission ... causes hurt to any person or damage to any
-- property"; (4) $10,000 or 3 years.
GIVEN `wilfully tampered` IS A BOOLEAN, `danger or damage likely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tampering is an offence` IF `wilfully tampered` AND `danger or damage likely`

GIVEN `rash or negligent` IS A BOOLEAN, `hurt or damage caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `negligent handling is an offence` IF `rash or negligent` AND `hurt or damage caused`

§§ `32 -- removing labels and marks`

-- s 32(1): "An individual commits an offence if he or she, without reasonable excuse, defaces, obliterates or removes" an approval
-- label, an alteration-approved label or a registration mark "when it is lawfully affixed to an EV charger".
GIVEN `defaced or removed a label or mark` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was lawfully affixed` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removing a label is an offence` IF
    `defaced or removed a label or mark` AND `it was lawfully affixed` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `36 -- ignoring a defect warning`

-- s 36(1): a registered responsible person or a person with charge and control who is given a s 35 defect notice "commits an
-- offence if the person, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with the warning" (stop charging, do not supply, install
-- or certify until rectified). (2): "$2,000 for each EV charger ... subject to a maximum of $20,000" and $250 a day continuing.
GIVEN `number of chargers` IS A NUMBER, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for ignoring a defect warning` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (2000 TIMES `number of chargers`) 20000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `2 -- repeat offender`

-- s 2: a "repeat offender" is convicted of an offence and "has been convicted or found guilty of the same offence on at least one
-- other earlier occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before" the current conviction. Five years exactly is
-- treated as within (the text does not settle the boundary).
GIVEN `earlier conviction for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `years between the convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender` IF
    `earlier conviction for the same offence` AND `years between the convictions` AT MOST 5

§§ `6, 18, 20, 23, 24, 27, 29, 30, 32, 39 -- tiered penalties`

-- Each of these offences has four fine ceilings: individual, individual repeat offender, non-individual, non-individual repeat
-- offender; individuals also face imprisonment, doubled for a repeat offender. From the text:
--   s 6(3)  supply of a non-homologated charger      $20,000 / 24 months; repeat $40,000 / 48 months; others $40,000; repeat $80,000
--   s 18(3) charging with an unregistered charger     $5,000 / 6 months;   repeat $10,000 / 12 months; others $10,000; repeat $20,000
--   s 20(4) registration mark not affixed             $1,000 / 3 months;   repeat $2,000 / 6 months;   others $2,500;  repeat $5,000
--   s 23(3) certifying a non-homologated charger      $10,000 / 12 months; repeat $20,000 / 24 months; others $20,000; repeat $40,000
--   s 24(2) installing a non-homologated fixed charger $20,000 / 24 months; repeat $40,000 / 48 months; others $40,000; repeat $80,000
--   s 27(3) registration not transferred              $1,000 / 3 months;   repeat $2,000 / 6 months;   others $2,500;  repeat $5,000
--   s 29(2) improper use                              $5,000 / 6 months;   repeat $10,000 / 12 months; others $10,000; repeat $20,000
--   s 30(3) improper charging                         $5,000 / 6 months;   repeat $10,000 / 12 months; others $10,000; repeat $20,000
--   s 32(4) causing removal of a label                $5,000 / 6 months;   repeat $10,000 / 12 months; others $10,000; repeat $20,000
--   s 39(3) breach of a safety and security directive $20,000 / 24 months; repeat $40,000 / 48 months; others $40,000; repeat $80,000
-- The non-individual ceiling is twice the individual one everywhere except ss 20 and 27, where it is two and a half times.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `supplying a non-homologated charger`
    `charging with an unregistered charger`
    `not affixing the registration mark`
    `certifying a non-homologated charger`
    `installing a non-homologated fixed charger`
    `not transferring the registration`
    `improper use of a charger`
    `improper charging`
    `causing removal of a label`
    `breaching a safety and security directive`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual base fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supplying a non-homologated charger` THEN 20000
    WHEN `charging with an unregistered charger` THEN 5000
    WHEN `not affixing the registration mark` THEN 1000
    WHEN `certifying a non-homologated charger` THEN 10000
    WHEN `installing a non-homologated fixed charger` THEN 20000
    WHEN `not transferring the registration` THEN 1000
    WHEN `improper use of a charger` THEN 5000
    WHEN `improper charging` THEN 5000
    WHEN `causing removal of a label` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-individual base fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not affixing the registration mark` THEN 2500
    WHEN `not transferring the registration` THEN 2500
    OTHERWISE 2 TIMES `the individual base fine` `the offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual base months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supplying a non-homologated charger` THEN 24
    WHEN `charging with an unregistered charger` THEN 6
    WHEN `not affixing the registration mark` THEN 3
    WHEN `certifying a non-homologated charger` THEN 12
    WHEN `installing a non-homologated fixed charger` THEN 24
    WHEN `not transferring the registration` THEN 3
    WHEN `improper use of a charger` THEN 6
    WHEN `improper charging` THEN 6
    WHEN `causing removal of a label` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 24

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `offender is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `offender is an individual`
    THEN (IF `offender is a repeat offender` THEN 2 TIMES `the individual base fine` `the offence` ELSE `the individual base fine` `the offence`)
    ELSE (IF `offender is a repeat offender` THEN 2 TIMES `the non-individual base fine` `the offence` ELSE `the non-individual base fine` `the offence`)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `offender is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `offender is an individual`
    THEN (IF `offender is a repeat offender` THEN 2 TIMES `the individual base months` `the offence` ELSE `the individual base months` `the offence`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `81 -- composition`

-- s 81(1)(a): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for a sum "not exceeding the lower of" (i) "one
-- half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (ii) "$5,000". Which offences are prescribed was
-- not retrieved.
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling` MEANS `the smaller of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `61, 62 -- when car parks must be wired for charging`

-- s 61(1): Part 8 applies to "defined works" in a development: (a) building works resulting in "the erection or re-erection of a
-- building"; (b) other building works that "would increase the approved gross floor area of the development by at least 50%"
-- (or a lower prescribed percentage); (c) electrical work requiring approval to increase the approved electrical load, where the
-- load before is "more than 280kVA", or where it is 280kVA or less and the increase takes it "to more than 280kVA".
-- s 62(1): not (a) Government works on State land, (b) a public authority's works on its own land. (2): the charging-point
-- duty (ss 64(1)(b), 65(1)(b)) does not apply where the works "would result in fewer than 8 parking lots".
GIVEN `erects or re-erects a building` IS A BOOLEAN, `percent increase in gross floor area` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building works are defined works` IF
    `erects or re-erects a building` OR `percent increase in gross floor area` AT LEAST 50

GIVEN `approved load before in kVA` IS A NUMBER, `approved load after in kVA` IS A NUMBER, `needs approval to increase the load` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the electrical work is defined works` IF
    `needs approval to increase the load` AND
        (    `approved load before in kVA` GREATER THAN 280
         OR  `approved load after in kVA` GREATER THAN 280)

GIVEN `parking lots after the works` IS A NUMBER, `Government or public authority on its own land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `charging points must be installed` IF
    (NOT `Government or public authority on its own land`) AND `parking lots after the works` AT LEAST 8

§§ `65(4) -- the owner's 12 months`

-- s 65(4): the owner must install the infrastructure and charging points, and give the LTA the documents, within "12 months, or
-- such longer period as the LTA may approve in writing", after the switchgear is turned on or the increased load takes effect.
-- An LTA approval shorter than 12 months is ignored here: the text only allows a longer one.
GIVEN `months since switch-on or load increase` IS A NUMBER, `months approved by the LTA` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is still in time` IF
    `months since switch-on or load increase` AT MOST `the larger of` 12 `months approved by the LTA`

§§ `68(2) -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 68(2): an appeal "must be in writing and specify the grounds" and be made "within 28 days after the date the decision appealed
-- against is given", or a longer period the Minister allows "for special reasons". (4) the decision must be complied with
-- meanwhile.
GIVEN `days since the decision was given` IS A NUMBER, `in writing with grounds` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister allowed more time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time and in form` IF
    `in writing with grounds` AND (`days since the decision was given` AT MOST 28 OR `Minister allowed more time`)
